<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73158" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁλκ-αῖος</span></b> ,, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁλκή</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>drawn along,</i>
			<i>towed,</i> of a ship (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁλκάς</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				268
			</span></i> : hence, <i>trailing, dragging,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σειρή,</span> of a serpent, ib.<i><span class="en">
				119
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτραπός</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				160
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					216
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
				Subst.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁλκαία</span></b> , 
				Ion.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁλκαίη</span></b> , ἡ, <i>tail,</i> because it is <i>trailed along,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				123
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				225
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.1614
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλκαία</span>
			, which Schn. writes in <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
			</span></i> ll. cc.).</div>
